road to zero  the impact of crashes  in 2020  318 people were killed and almost two  and a half thousand seriously injured on  new zealand's roads  we need to start doing things  differently everyone should be able to  get to where they're going safely  whether they're walking cycling driving  on a motorbike or using public transport  some members of our community see the  impacts that crashes can have way too  often  hi i'm kim munro i am a senior press  constable based in the rangara area i'm  attached to the strategic traffic unit  i've been with the police for 17 years  over the years i've dealt with several  crashes and a lot of them have been  quite serious and even resulting in  death the impact of dealing with  families is huge we are all human and we  do make mistakes but unfortunately those  mistakes  can have devastating effects  so i lost my family in a fatal crash  many years ago when i was six years old  so it's had a huge impact on my life  and now i like to  give back and try and help other people  not go through those consequences  we do or make mistakes but things like  taking your time on the roads wearing  your seat belt not driving impaired not  driving with alcohol or drugs and also  putting that cell phone down would make  a huge difference  so none of us want to be the reason for  a crash we can all help each other out  by being a little bit more patient  and courteous on the road and just take  that extra time  we all need to look out for each other  no one wants to be the reason someone  gets hurt on our roads  we can all make a difference  [Music]
 

